      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "I did a more detailed review, and this is looking great. I guess we might have missed you, so we'll probably have to finish this ourselves, but if you're able to help, one thing that would be very nice would be a clearer documentation of the implementation-defined cases.\r\n\r\nFrom what I can see we have the following:\r\n\r\n- _sourceOrigin_ or _destinationOrigin_ are non-HTTP(S), BCG swap is optional. https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10842\r\n- \"browser UI\", BCG swap is optional. Part of https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/6356 although that's broader\r\n- BCG size is 1. The spec has clear notes about this one.\r\n- _subtreesToSearch_ choice is either (top, window) or (top, ..., window). **Can you give us more detail on why this is implementation-defined?** Like, does Chromium choose differently depending on certain circumstances, and if so, which circumstances? Do you know what would motivate one choice or another?\r\n- Optionally check \"allowed by sandboxing to navigate\" (in two places). **Why is this optional?**\r\n- Implementation-defined order for searching through the BCG by name. This is pretty clear from the spec, but in the interest of maybe nailing this down in the future, can you tell us what Chromium picks?\r\n",
    "state": "COMMENTED",
